I have two problems with PC-NetHack 3.0pl6, both related to
running it on a non-IBM MS-DOS machine (an HP 150, for those who
are curious).

1.  You can't turn off standout once you turn off color.  On the
AT clone at work I just leave color on, but on my home machine
highlighting doesn't work the way it does on VT100s and
such--once you highlight an area it stays highlighted until you
explicitly cancel it.  So moving around leaves a trail of
highlighted character cells.  I can just put a null so capability
in my termcap, but feh.

2.  The most important impediment--the overlay manager assumes
that you must be running DOS 3.3 since it tries to find the
executable file name after the end of the environment.  This
bombs on my DOS 2.01 home machine.  If I get desperate enough
I'll patch the binary to get around it, but . . .

Otherwise the pl6 binary is very nice and does run faster than
the pl3 binary that I helped Norm Meluch beta-test.
